   "date": "2021-07-02T03:14:24Z",
   "subject": "Re: openCR 2.0.2",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>That particular backward compatibility problem arises because openCR 2.0 added the details argument &#39;minimumage&#39; and the function openCR.make.newdata did not allow for old models in which it wasn&#39;t defined. I think it would be fixed by inserting a value thus<br></div><div><br></div><div>oldfit$details$minimumage &lt;- 0</div><div><br></div><div>As this shows, the code has not been tested for backward compatibility and there may be other issues. It&#39;s good to catch this now, and I&#39;ll run some other checks.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Murray<br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
